---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Rent vs Buy HOA Fees (Condo and community costs)";
const description =
  "How HOA dues affect rent vs buy comparisons, including what they cover and how to model them. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-02-17";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/rent-vs-buy-hoa-fees" lastUpdated={lastUpdated}>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">HOA fees</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>HOA fees in rent vs buy comparisons</h1>
    <p>
      HOA dues can materially change monthly homeowner costs, especially for condos or planned communities. This guide shows how to
      model HOA fees and avoid double counting.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/rent-vs-buy-calculator">Rent vs buy calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/rent-vs-buy-costs-to-include">Costs to include</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/rent-vs-buy">Rent vs buy topic hub</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Rent vs buy inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Holding period (time horizon).</li>
      <li>Mortgage rate, down payment, and closing/selling costs.</li>
      <li>Rent growth and home appreciation assumptions.</li>
      <li>Maintenance, taxes, insurance, HOA, and investment return.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">What HOA fees typically cover</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Shared maintenance (roof, exterior, common areas).</li>
      <li>Amenities (pool, gym, landscaping, security).</li>
      <li>Reserves for future repairs, depending on the HOA budget.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How to model HOA fees</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use the current monthly HOA amount in the homeowner costs.</li>
      <li>Check if HOA covers items you would otherwise include as maintenance.</li>
      <li>Plan for potential increases over time if the HOA history shows growth.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Documents to review</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>HOA budget and reserve study.</li>
      <li>Recent meeting notes for planned projects.</li>
      <li>Special assessment history.</li>
      <li>What insurance is covered by the HOA master policy.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Avoid double counting</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      If the HOA covers exterior maintenance or major repairs, reduce your separate maintenance assumption so you do not double count
      the same costs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Ignoring HOA dues entirely.</li>
      <li>Assuming HOA dues never increase.</li>
      <li>Counting HOA fees and full maintenance at the same time.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Historical HOA increase rate or planned hikes.</li>
      <li>Reserve health and likelihood of special assessments.</li>
      <li>What maintenance is already covered by HOA dues.</li>
      <li>Insurance gaps between HOA master policy and your policy.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">What if HOA dues cover most maintenance?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Reduce the separate maintenance assumption to cover only what is not included in the HOA budget.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Should I model special assessments?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      If special assessments are possible, add a buffer to maintenance or include a one-time cost scenario.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/rent-vs-buy-calculator">Rent vs buy calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/rent-vs-buy-costs-to-include">Costs to include</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/rent-vs-buy-maintenance-estimate">Maintenance estimate</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/what-is-piti">What is PITI?</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/rent-vs-buy-calculator">Run the calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/rent-vs-buy-costs-to-include">Costs to include</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/rent-vs-buy-break-even">Break-even guide</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-02-17</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>



